{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Surface\nGitHub Actions, repo navapbc/rebar, workflow **Test Suite (mirror)** (scheduled/dispatch, non-blocking mirror tier), matrix `sweep (…)` jobs. Blocking core tiers pass on main; only the experimental `sweep` matrix is red.\n\n## Signatures (two distinct sub-failures)\n1. **sweep (windows)** — `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'fcntl'` at collection; Windows tier cannot collect.\n2. **sweep (py3.14)** — `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py::test_a_contended_fcntl_leg_reads_as_held` fails `RuntimeError: Network access is forbidden in unit/scripts tests`.\n\n(The `sweep (macos, full suite)` / `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` legs are the recurrence of closed `e3e0-2e7c-b280-4b4a`, tracked there — not this ticket.)\n\n## Severity: P3\nMirror/experimental tier — non-blocking. CI-hygiene / cross-platform-portability signal.\n\n---\n\n## Fix plan (Phase 2) — two independent root causes, confirmed in Phase 1 RCA comment\n\n**RC#1 (Windows collection blackout):** 4 modules do an *unconditional* module-top `import fcntl`, violating the codebase's established portability-guard invariant (6 sibling modules already `try/except ImportError → None`). Because `import rebar` transitively hits `doctor_locks.py:69`, ALL collection dies on non-POSIX. Fix = guard the 4 imports (collectability only; Windows fcntl *locking* is out of scope — non-support-target). Zero behavior change on POSIX.\n\n**RC#2 (py3.14 red):** the autouse network guard (`tests/conftest.py`) patches `socket.socket.connect` for ALL families; py3.14's Linux default start-method change `fork`→`forkserver` makes `multiprocessing` use an AF_UNIX (local IPC) connect, which the guard wrongly rejects. Fix = narrow the guard to block only AF_INET/AF_INET6 (real network), allow local IPC.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_store/lock.py` — `import fcntl` guarded; POSIX behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py` — `import fcntl` guarded.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/reducer/marker.py` — `import fcntl` guarded.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py` — `import fcntl` guarded.\n- [ ] RED→GREEN: the 4 modules import under simulated non-POSIX (`sys.modules['fcntl']=None`); `import rebar` succeeds.\n- [ ] Structural guard `scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py` (AST; portable, wired into `make lint`) fails on any unguarded module-level `import fcntl` in `src/rebar`; ships true-positive + true-negative + refactor-survival tests.\n- [ ] Step7 test siblings: `tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py` and `tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py` use `pytest.importorskip(\"fcntl\")` so they skip (not error) on non-POSIX.\n- [ ] `tests/conftest.py` — network guard blocks only AF_INET/AF_INET6; AF_UNIX allowed.\n- [ ] RED→GREEN: a `forkserver` `multiprocessing.Process` starts under the guard; a real AF_INET connect is still blocked (teeth).\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the affected tests pass.\n\n### Portability (project.portability)\nThe structural guard is a stdlib-only AST script wired into `make lint` — no CI provider required, runnable locally and under any CI. The network-guard narrowing is interpreter/OS-agnostic (family check).\n\n## Provenance\nPeriodic ops-error sweep. `caused_by` → `13ad-4c6f-4074-4f43` (added both red tiers). See Phase 1 RCA comment for full mechanism proofs + attribution."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788150705583580790,"uuid":"1715f5ba-d08a-4659-b3fd-9a368851c287"}